- low capacity factor or severe curtailment;
- short operating life or early repowering;
- unusually large concrete foundations or difficult offshore installation;
- high-carbon electricity used for steel, cement, and component manufacturing;
- long-distance, inefficient transport;
- large transmission and storage additions;
- allocating system infrastructure entirely to wind;
- comparing wind with an efficient gas plant rather than coal;
- accounting for methane leakage in a consistent way.

