So my defensible conclusion should have been:

> For typical utility-scale projects, published lifecycle studies generally find lower greenhouse-gas emissions per delivered kWh for wind than for fossil generation. However, headline values are not representative of every project, and real-world project- or system-level results can be considerably higher.

I would not claim that every wind project has lower lifetime emissions than every fossil alternative. If your colleagues are referring to actual project carbon inventories, low-output sites, repowering, offshore construction, or whole-system accounting, their experience may be identifying limitations that the simplified comparison hides.

