You’re right—I was answering a weaker question than the one asked.

I treated **“can operate”** as “the vehicle remains functional,” whereas **“operate effectively in extreme temperatures”** should include acceptable range, charging time, power availability, HVAC performance, uptime, and reliability. On that standard, my answer was too reassuring.

