> EVs can be engineered to function in hot and cold climates, but they do not necessarily operate effectively under extreme conditions without suitable thermal management, preconditioning, charging infrastructure, and operating margins. In practice, extreme cold is often particularly difficult because it simultaneously reduces battery output, increases heating demand, restricts regenerative braking, and slows charging. Extreme heat can cause cooling loads, charging derating, and accelerated degradation.

